      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change also allows the test case to pass. W/o it, checkForIntersection() incorrectly thought there was no intersection and fell back on intersectEdgePair\u0027s topology correction. Since there was a real intersection, the adjustment made in intersectEdgePair was pretty drastic, causing the edges to become out of order. The below fix for intersectEdgePair fixes the out-of-order issue/crash, but would still result in a less-than-ideal simplification.\n\nI had the midpoint update backwards for the binary searching along the segments. If s or t were \u003e 1/2, we want to search from the midpoint to the end vertex so the first vertex should be set to the midpoint.",
